 computers (virtual or on dedicated hardware), and data storage space. Infr=
astructure as a Service provides you with the highest level of flexibility =
and management control over your IT resources and is most similar to existi=
ng IT resources that many IT departments and developers are familiar with t=
oday.</p>

<p><strong>Platform as a Service (PaaS)</strong> - Platform as a Service (P=
aaS) as a service removes the need for organizations to manage the underlyi=
ng infrastructure (usually hardware and operating systems) and allow you to=
 focus on the deployment and management of your applications. This helps yo=
u be more efficient as you don=E2=80=99t need to worry about resource procu=
rement, capacity planning, software maintenance, patching, or any of the ot=
her undifferentiated heavy lifting involved in running your application.</p=
